// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 10-temporal-validity
// facility: rule.temporal.elision `[Result-Source-Probe-Only]` (D-0312): a closure capturing the other parameter keeps it when its call's result is kept; conf.result-source-kept-captured
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.result-source-kept (static)
//
// A closure capturing `b` and called where its result is kept: the
// result of a call through a `fn` value keeps what the closure holds.
// (A closure whose result is only measured keeps only what its body
// does, report 183, CHG-0479.)

import std;

fn bad(StringView a, StringView b) : StringView from a
{
    auto f = [b]() : StringView { b };
    if (StringView::len(a) == 0)
    {
        return f();
    }
    a
}

fn main()
{
    printf("%s\n", bad("xyz", "y"));
}
